      <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><span><span>The fair value of stock options issued in years prior to December 31, 2024 were determined at the time of issuance using the Black-Scholes option pricing model. The stock options issued in the year ended December 31, 2025 were determined at the time of issuance using a Monte Carlo simulation incorporating Brownian motion, which simulates a distribution of stock prices for the Company throughout the term of the stock options, based on certain assumptions of stock price behavior. The significant inputs to the valuation include a <ix:nonNumeric id="Fxbrl_20260427131456087" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedTerm1" contextRef="C_20250101to20251231_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" format="ixt-sec:duryear">10</ix:nonNumeric>-year term to expiration, the closing price of the Common Shares on the December 19, 2025 grant date ($<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260427132157020" name="us-gaap:SharePrice" contextRef="C_20251231_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="USD_Per_Share" scale="0" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">7.31</ix:nonFraction>), a risk-free rate of return of <ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260427132210886" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsRiskFreeInterestRate" contextRef="C_20250101to20251231_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="Pure" scale="-2" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">4.12</ix:nonFraction>% per annum, and a volatility of <ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260427132222632" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedVolatilityRate" contextRef="C_20250101to20251231_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="Pure" scale="-2" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">102</ix:nonFraction>% based on the historical volatility of Solana calculated from its historical daily returns. The stock options issued in the six months ended June 30, 2026 were determined at the time of issuance using the Black-Scholes option pricing model with significant inputs including a <ix:nonNumeric id="Fxbrl_20260727134057760" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedTerm1" contextRef="C_20260101to20260630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" format="ixt-sec:duryear">10</ix:nonNumeric>-year term to expiration, the closing price of the Common Shares on the May 5, 2026 grant date ($<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260727134512840" name="us-gaap:SharePrice" contextRef="C_20260630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="USD_Per_Share" scale="0" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">5.10</ix:nonFraction>), a risk-free rate of return of <ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260727134523991" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsRiskFreeInterestRate" contextRef="C_20260101to20260630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="Pure" scale="-2" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">3.60</ix:nonFraction>% per annum, and a volatility of <ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260727134532228" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedVolatilityRate" contextRef="C_20260101to20260630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="Pure" scale="-2" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">100</ix:nonFraction>% based on the historical volatility of Solana calculated from its historical daily returns.</span></span></span></span></p>
      <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><span><span>The total expense related to the options granted in the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 was $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260427151554843" name="us-gaap:StockOptionPlanExpense" contextRef="C_20260401to20260630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">1.6</ix:nonFraction> million and $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260727134646910" name="us-gaap:StockOptionPlanExpense" contextRef="C_20260101to20260630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">4.3</ix:nonFraction> million, respectively (2025 - $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260727134705443" name="us-gaap:StockOptionPlanExpense" contextRef="C_20250401to20250630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-6" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen"><ix:nonFraction id="Ffid_936" name="us-gaap:StockOptionPlanExpense" contextRef="C_20250101to20250630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockOptionMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-6" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen">nil</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>). This expense is included in the share based compensation line on the unaudited condensed interim consolidated statements of loss and comprehensive loss. The options granted in 2025 vest based on the Company's volume weighted average price ("VWAP") of the Company's common shares as follows:</span></span></span></span></p>
