      <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><span><span><strong>STOCK APPRECIATION RIGHTS ("SARs")</strong></span></span></span></span></p>
      <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><span><span><span><span><ix:nonNumeric id="Fxbrl_20260427134012920" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardDescription" contextRef="C_20260101to20260630_usgaapAwardTypeAxis_usgaapStockAppreciationRightsSARSMember">SARs grant a right to receive, upon exercise thereof, the excess of the fair market value of one Common Share on the date of exercise over the grant price of the SAR. The grant price of a SAR shall not be less than 100% of the fair market value of a Common Share on the date of the grant. SARs generally vest over a period of zero to three years and have a term of ten or eleven years.</ix:nonNumeric>&#160;The SARS granted by the Company to date are only payable in Common Shares and have no cash payments options.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>
